 "title": "Register of Deeds - JOHNSON COUNTY, NEBRASKA",
 "text": "Register of Deeds - JOHNSON COUNTY, NEBRASKA\nJOHNSON COUNTY, NEBRASKA\n|\n|\n|\n|\n|\nHome\nCounty Offices\nOther Links\nContacts\nCounty Boards\nREGISTER OF DEEDS\nDuties:\n|\nKATHLEEN NIEVEEN is the Johnson County Register of Deeds. The Register of Deeds has the power to take acknowledgments, administer oaths, and certify the same by his or her signature. The Register must keep a book in which every instrument filed for record in her office is entered and an official seal. The Register of Deeds may appoint one or more deputies for whose acts the Register will be responsible.\n|\nOffice Hours:\n|\nHours for the Register of Deeds: 8:00 a.m. to 12:30 p.m. and 1:00 p.m. to 4:30 p.m., Monday - Friday\n​\n|\nContact Information:\n|\nMailing Address: P.O. Box 416, Tecumseh, NE 68450\nPhone Number: 402-335-6300\nFax Number: 402-335-6311\nclerk@johnsoncounty.ne.gov\n​\n|\nContact Register of Deeds\nCounty Assessor\nCounty Attorney\nCounty Clerk\nCounty Sheriff\nCounty Treasurer\nDistrict Court Clerk\nEmergency Management Agency\nHighway Superintendent\nJohnson County Extension\nRegister of Deeds\nSurveyor\nVeteran's Service Office\nZoning Administrator\nPowered by\nCreate your own unique website with customizable templates.\nGet Started",
